Explain what changes between delivered material and usable feed (@cs-conditioning: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @chemical-supply-systems, #source "../sources/Caustic-Soda-Handbook-OxyChem.lingua#r_1MRFTA19NDBFBQXC69CCRQPAME", #source "../sources/Oxygen-Pipeline-and-Piping-Systems-EIGA.lingua#r_7BBE969N5JQJES1KG9AKNBEZBV", #source "../sources/High-Purity-Polymer-Delivery-Components-SEMI.lingua#r_4CJR70PGX15X3VQENBZ0S1RA25", #source "../sources/Pharmaceutical-Starting-Materials-WHO.lingua#r_7H51215T44S69TD3R0499VMTTY", #chemical-supply-systems "../../../../inquiry/quantitative-literacy/practice/Mass-and-component-balances.lingua#r_163GVDJGRJ1DD4JT2398GM371H") { r_7B2CJQGS5NV8WKM09952PT3VHC
**Read:** [Caustic Soda Handbook — OxyChem](../sources/Caustic-Soda-Handbook-OxyChem.lingua#r_1MRFTA19NDBFBQXC69CCRQPAME), complete relevant concentration, property and handling sections; [Oxygen Pipeline and Piping Systems — EIGA Doc 13/20](../sources/Oxygen-Pipeline-and-Piping-Systems-EIGA.lingua#r_7BBE969N5JQJES1KG9AKNBEZBV), complete applicable conditioning, equipment, cleaning and operation sections; [High-purity polymer materials and chemical-delivery components — SEMI F57](../sources/High-Purity-Polymer-Delivery-Components-SEMI.lingua#r_4CJR70PGX15X3VQENBZ0S1RA25), the complete authorized component/qualification methods for the relevant case; [Good trade and distribution practices for pharmaceutical starting materials — WHO](../sources/Pharmaceutical-Starting-Materials-WHO.lingua#r_7H51215T44S69TD3R0499VMTTY), complete changed-material and documentation sections.

Identify the boundary between a supplied chemical and the feed actually entering the user's operation. Dilution, filtration, drying, vaporisation, warming, blending, activation or purification can change composition, physical state, evidence and the quantity still usable. Treat each operation as a process with a purpose, inputs, outputs and limits.

For an aqueous input, separate an exact quantity/concentration calculation from the actual mixing, heat and contact-system questions. For a gas, connect storage and vaporisation with pressure/flow, contaminant control and usable reserve. For an electronic chemical, identify which contaminants a particular filter or conditioning operation can and cannot remove. “Purification” is not a guarantee that every required property has been established.

Construct a delivery-to-use account with representative sampling and a declared release point. Decide whether a supplier's certificate still represents the material after the intervening operation. Include utility, equipment and skilled-work requirements and the consequences of their interruption. Compare receiving a ready-to-use grade with conditioning a different accepted supply on site. Use the shared chemical-process Records for the transformations; here defend the interface and evidence needed to rely on the resulting feed.

